# Two Null Summoners: each one's threshold ability casts "the exiled card", the card its own enters ability exiled (CR 607.2a),
# and only while that permanent is on the battlefield (CR 604.1, 611.3a). Bot1 casts both on turn one: the first exiles Bot2's
# Shock, the second one of its Lightning Bolts. Bot2 bolts the first Summoner on turn two. On turn three Brain Freeze mills
# three, so Bot1's graveyard holds exactly seven cards (two Black Lotuses, the Summoner, Brain Freeze and three Islands):
# threshold, at its least (CR 207.2c). With Mox Sapphire open the Shock, whose Summoner is gone, can't be cast; the Bolt, by the
# Summoner still there, can (its {R} paid with blue, CR 609.4b), and it hits Bot2.

